[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AttributionEntry" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://attribution/attribution_entry.gd" id="1_entry"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_entry")
id = "quaternius_poly_pizza_nature"
creator = "Quaternius"
source_name = "Standalone Nature/Crops Models"
source_version = "Downloaded individually via poly.pizza model pages, 2026-08-16 (exact
retrieval date recorded, unlike quaternius_poly_pizza_characters.tres's undated set)."
creator_url = "https://quaternius.com"
source_url = "https://poly.pizza/u/Quaternius"
support_url = "https://www.patreon.com/quaternius"
license_name = "CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication"
license_url = "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
license_file = "res://assets/licenses/Quaternius_UltimateAnimatedAnimals_License.txt"
attribution_required = false
required_notice = ""
conditions = ""
assets_used = PackedStringArray("Crops (poly.pizza/m/Ro6K0Yg7mx)", "Wheat (poly.pizza/m/lPspzfC8Pu)")
per_file_licensing = false
notes = "CC0 — crediting is courtesy, not compliance. Reuses
Quaternius_UltimateAnimatedAnimals_License.txt as license_file rather than duplicating an
identical generic CC0 boilerplate under a new filename, same convention as every other
Quaternius entry in this project (the text is not pack-specific).

Sourced for the 2026-08-16 terrain look-pass (grass/forest/rock/water/cultivated_field/
wild_grass). Each model's exact poly.pizza page URL is recorded in assets_used above
(unlike quaternius_poly_pizza_characters.tres, whose five files predate this convention) —
confirmed Quaternius creator + CC0 license on each page before download, per
asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate.

Per-asset destination and use:
  - Rock_2.glb (\"Rock\") -> project/assets/terrain/rock_2/ -> used in RockCluster2.tscn,
    RockCluster3.tscn, RockCluster4.tscn.
  - RockMediumMoss.glb (\"Rock Medium\") -> project/assets/terrain/rock_medium_moss/ ->
    used in RockCluster3.tscn as the mossy anchor piece.
  - RocksCluster.glb (\"Rocks\", a pre-modeled 3-rock group) ->
    project/assets/terrain/rocks_cluster/ -> used in RockCluster4.tscn.
  - GrassTufts.glb (\"Grass\") -> project/assets/terrain/grass_tufts/ -> IMPORTED BUT NOT
    WIRED. Its two internal mesh objects (Grass_Large_Extruded, Grass_Small) sit ~1.37
    tile-units apart in the source file's own local space (confirmed by AABB measurement,
    not assumed) — an artifact of how this file was assembled upstream, not a per-tile
    prop pair. Instancing the whole file at tile scale would place one tuft off in empty
    space well outside the tile; safely extracting just one internal node from a hand-
    authored .tscn risks exactly the \"silently corrupts the scene\" failure mode
    asset-import-pipeline.md warns about for scene-editing tools, so this was left
    unwired rather than forced. Available for a future pass if a human wants to invest
    editor time in splitting it.
  - CropsPlot.glb (\"Crops\") -> project/assets/terrain/crops_plot/ -> used in
    CultivatedCropsPlot.tscn.
  - Wheat.glb (\"Wheat\") -> project/assets/terrain/wheat/ -> used in
    CultivatedWheatRow.tscn.
  - PineTree.glb (\"Pine Tree\") -> project/assets/terrain/pine_tree/ -> used in
    PineTree.tscn, wired as forest.tres's 3rd model_scenes entry (2026-08-16, same-day
    follow-up after a human eyeball pass on the look-pass above reported forest not
    reading as alternating between assets — CommonTree1/CommonTree2 read as
    indistinguishable at the fixed camera pitch; Pine Tree is a genuinely different
    conifer silhouette, not a third round-canopy \"common tree\").

DISTINCT FROM quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres and
quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres: those are two specific named/versioned pack
downloads with their own pack pages; these six are standalone poly.pizza model downloads
whose parent pack (if any) was not identified, same relationship as
quaternius_poly_pizza_characters.tres has to the two named animal packs.

PRUNED 2026-09-08 -- assets_used now records what the SHIPPED BUILD contains, not everything ever
imported from this pack. The 2026-09-08 Forest MegaKit standardisation, the house cull and the
Snowfield retirement unwired part of this pack from gameplay. project/export_presets.cfg now
drops those files from all three presets via exclude_filter, so they are no longer distributed
and no longer credited here. THE FILES REMAIN IN THE REPO under project/assets/ and their import
tests still run -- if one is rewired it must be added back to assets_used AND removed from
exclude_filter, or it will ship uncredited.
Removed in this pass: Rock, Rock Medium, Rocks, Grass and Pine Tree (5 in all).
What survives is CropsPlot.glb and Wheat.glb, still composed into CultivatedCropsPlot.tscn and
CultivatedWheatRow.tscn. CORRECTS A CLAIM MADE ELSEWHERE: assets/terrain/pine_1/Pine1.tscn's
header calls the removed PineTree the project's only Poly Pizza asset. It was not -- these two
crop models are from this same standalone-download set and still ship. GrassTufts was already
recorded above as imported but never wired."
